0051 — export the raster revision, the half of "nothing to repaint" that
`ui_draw_hash` does not carry.

`ui_draw_hash` hashes the DrawList's words, and its doc comment offers it to
browser hosts as a dirty signal for skipping a render. The words are not
everything a raster reads. A TEX_QUAD carries a texture HANDLE, and the walk
emits it without resolving it (`draw.rs`, `emit_tex_quad`), so freeing the
texture an image is bound to leaves the words as they were while the raster
resolves the handle to nothing and the image is gone. A font atlas loaded
over a slot is the same shape: a GLYPH_RUN names the slot, not the coverage.
The core already knows this. `Ui::raster_revision` moves on every texture
upload and free, font atlas load, asset load and style table load, and
`damage::DamageTracker::prepare` repaints in full unless the words, that
revision and the render target are all unchanged. Nothing exported the
revision, so a wasm host could compare two of the three.

`ui_raster_revision()` returns it. `hosts/web/wasm-ops.js` exposes it as
`rasterRevision`, null on a build that predates the export, the way
`drawHash` is feature-detected. The doc comment on `ui_draw_hash` now says
what a host that skips on it must compare as well.

Why pocket-motion needs it: `render` skips the raster of a frame whose draw
list and raster revision equal the previous frame's and delivers the previous
frame's pixels (`src/render/reuse.ts`). Keyed on the words alone, the reuse
would rest on which ops this repository's host and guests happen to call
after mount, rather than on the condition the core states.

The export adds no code to any render path, so no pixel can move: every
composition in the motion repository's digest ledger traced to its recorded
digest on a core built with it.

Test, seen red under the edit named:

- `engine/core/src/tests.rs`
  `freeing_a_bound_texture_moves_the_raster_revision_and_not_the_draw_list`:
  an image's texture freed after it was drawn leaves the words equal, moves
  the revision, and the raster no longer draws the image. Red with
  `free_texture`'s `bump_raster_revision()` removed.

diff --git a/engine/wasm/src/lib.rs b/engine/wasm/src/lib.rs
index a35e0ea..9c98314 100644
--- a/engine/wasm/src/lib.rs
+++ b/engine/wasm/src/lib.rs
@@ -561,11 +561,29 @@ pub extern "C" fn ui_tick() {
 /// rasterizing the framebuffer. Browser hosts use this as the same dirty
 /// signal as pocket-widget's EmbeddedUi: a settled guest can keep ticking
 /// while skipping the expensive software render and texture upload.
+///
+/// The words are not everything a raster reads. A TEX_QUAD carries a texture
+/// handle, not the texels, and the walk does not resolve it: free the texture
+/// an image is bound to and the words stay the same while the raster draws
+/// nothing there. A host that skips a render on an equal hash compares
+/// [`ui_raster_revision`] as well, which is the pair the core's own
+/// `DamageTracker` compares.
 #[no_mangle]
 pub extern "C" fn ui_draw_hash() -> u64 {
     draw_hash(&ui().draw().words)
 }
 
+/// The core's raster revision: a counter every texture upload and free, font
+/// atlas load and style table load moves (`Ui::raster_revision`). Equal draw
+/// list words, an equal revision and the same render target are the core's
+/// condition for a frame needing no repaint (`damage::DamageTracker::prepare`);
+/// this exports the half of it the draw-list hash does not carry. Read it
+/// after `ui_draw_hash`: a walk may itself load what it draws.
+#[no_mangle]
+pub extern "C" fn ui_raster_revision() -> u64 {
+    ui().raster_revision()
+}
+
 /// The same hash for the auxiliary surface's DrawList, so a host with a second
 /// screen redraws it when its content changes. Returns 0 when the instance has
 /// no auxiliary surface.
diff --git a/engine/core/src/tests.rs b/engine/core/src/tests.rs
index 5dfd45e..97f15bb 100644
--- a/engine/core/src/tests.rs
+++ b/engine/core/src/tests.rs
@@ -7611,3 +7611,43 @@ fn shutter_value_at_is_tick_timelines() {
         assert_eq!(tx(&ui, n).to_bits(), expect.to_bits(), "clock {c}");
     }
 }
+
+/// The fact `ui_raster_revision` is exported for. An image whose texture is
+/// freed keeps its TEX_QUAD — the walk emits the handle without resolving it —
+/// so the draw list's words do not move, while the raster resolves the handle
+/// to nothing and the image is gone from the frame. A host that skips a
+/// raster on an equal draw-list hash and nothing else reuses a picture the
+/// core would no longer draw; the revision is what moves.
+#[test]
+fn freeing_a_bound_texture_moves_the_raster_revision_and_not_the_draw_list() {
+    let mut ui = Ui::new();
+    let red = [255u8, 0, 0, 255].repeat(16 * 16);
+    let tex = ui.upload_texture(&red, 16, 16, spec::psm::PSM_8888);
+    let img = ui.create_node(spec::NodeType::Image as u8);
+    ui.set_prop(img, spec::prop::WIDTH, 16.0);
+    ui.set_prop(img, spec::prop::HEIGHT, 16.0);
+    ui.insert_before(spec::ROOT_ID, img, 0);
+    ui.set_image(img, tex);
+    ui.tick();
+
+    let fb_len = spec::SCREEN_W as usize * spec::SCREEN_H as usize * 4;
+    let before = ui.draw().words.clone();
+    let revision = ui.raster_revision();
+    let mut shown = alloc::vec![0u8; fb_len];
+    crate::raster::render(&ui, &before, &mut shown);
+    assert_eq!(&shown[..4], &[255, 0, 0, 255], "the image is drawn before the free");
+
+    ui.free_texture(tex);
+    let after = ui.draw().words.clone();
+    assert_eq!(after, before, "the walk emits a freed handle unchanged");
+    assert_ne!(ui.raster_revision(), revision, "the free moves the raster revision");
+    let mut gone = alloc::vec![0u8; fb_len];
+    crate::raster::render(&ui, &after, &mut gone);
+    assert_ne!(&gone[..4], &[255, 0, 0, 255], "the raster draws nothing for a freed handle");
+
+    // Drawing again moves nothing: a walk over unchanged state is not a
+    // resource change.
+    let revision = ui.raster_revision();
+    let _ = ui.draw();
+    assert_eq!(ui.raster_revision(), revision);
+}
